---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';
import '../styles/home-device.css';
---

<Base title="TAR v6 — One order, end to end" themeColor="#10192b">
<header class="nav"><a class="brand" href="#top"><span>T</span>TAR <em>v6 / real-work walkthrough</em></a><nav><a href="#walk">Order journey</a><a href="#proof">What TAR protects</a><a href="/glossary">Visual glossary</a><a href="/architecture">Full architecture →</a></nav></header>
<main id="top"><section class="hero shell"><div><p class="kicker"><span></span>One complete example · Slice House</p><h1>Follow one order.<br>See the whole <i>system.</i></h1><p class="lede">Take Order #1042 from the counter to the customer’s hands. At every step, the left side shows what the person sees; the right side shows exactly what TAR saves and why.</p><a class="start" href="#walk">Begin with the customer <b>↓</b></a></div><div class="order-ticket"><div class="ticket-head"><span>SLICE HOUSE</span><span>10:14</span></div><div class="ticket-number">#1042</div><p>Priya · Takeaway</p><ul><li><span>2× Margherita</span><b>₹500</b></li><li><span>1× Garlic bread</span><b>₹120</b></li><li><span>Tax</span><b>₹31</b></li></ul><div class="ticket-total"><span>TOTAL</span><b>₹651</b></div><div class="ticket-status"><i></i><span id="hero-status">Ready to accept</span></div></div></section>
<section class="walk" id="walk"><div class="shell"><div class="walk-head"><div><p class="kicker light">The live order journey</p><h2>Do the work.<br>Watch TAR respond.</h2></div><p>Use Continue or choose any stage. The example follows v6’s declared food-order flow, including stock, the saved Run, receipt sending, and recovery.</p></div><div class="journey" id="journey" aria-label="Order stages"></div><div class="workbench"><section class="human-side"><div class="side-label"><span>ANDROID APP VIEW</span><b id="actor-label">Iniya · Cashier</b></div><div class="phone"><div class="phone-top"><span>10:14</span><b>Slice House</b><i id="avatar">I</i></div><div id="screen"></div><nav class="phone-bottom" aria-label="App tabs"><button data-home-tab="space" onclick="selectHomeTab('space')"><i>⌂</i><span>Space</span></button><button data-home-tab="inbox" onclick="selectHomeTab('inbox')"><i>⌁</i><span>Inbox</span></button><button data-home-tab="bots" onclick="selectHomeTab('bots')"><i>✦</i><span>Bots</span></button></nav></div></section><section class="tar-side"><div class="side-label"><span>WHAT TAR DOES</span><b id="system-label">Accept safely</b></div><div class="system-panel"><div class="system-intro"><p class="technical" id="technical-label">REGISTERED ACTION</p><h3 id="system-title">Check the order before accepting it.</h3><p id="system-copy"></p></div><div class="system-path" id="system-path"></div><div class="save-box"><span id="save-label">ONE ATOMIC SAVE</span><div id="save-items"></div></div></div></section></div><div class="walk-controls"><button id="back" class="back">← Previous</button><div><b id="step-count">1 / 8</b><span id="step-name">Customer order</span></div><button id="continue" class="continue">Accept order <b>→</b></button></div></div></section>
<section class="parallel shell"><div class="parallel-copy"><p class="kicker">One deliberate exception</p><h2>The receipt moves beside the order, not in front of it.</h2><p>A printer or messaging problem must not trap paid food at the counter. Checkout creates a durable receipt Delivery. The customer can receive the order while TAR confirms, retries, or sends the delivery to a person for review.</p></div><div class="parallel-map"><div class="fork"><span>Payment confirmed</span></div><div class="lane"><b>Order lane</b><i></i><span>Wait for handover</span><i></i><strong>Fulfilled</strong></div><div class="lane receipt"><b>Receipt lane</b><i></i><span>Send / reconcile</span><i></i><strong>Delivered</strong></div></div></section>
<section class="proof" id="proof"><div class="shell"><div class="proof-head"><p class="kicker light">Tap a real-world problem</p><h2>What TAR protects<br>when work gets messy.</h2></div><div class="problem-tabs" id="problem-tabs"></div><div class="problem-answer"><div class="problem-scene" id="problem-scene"></div><div><p class="technical" id="problem-rule"></p><h3 id="problem-title"></h3><p id="problem-copy"></p><div class="plain-rule" id="problem-plain"></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="roles shell"><div><p class="kicker">The same order, different windows</p><h2>Each person sees only what their job needs.</h2></div><div class="role-grid"><article><i class="violet">I</i><b>Iniya · Cashier</b><p>Price, payment, counter work. Can accept and checkout.</p></article><article><i class="orange">V</i><b>Velan · Kitchen</b><p>Products, quantities, preparation. No customer phone or payment fields.</p></article><article><i class="blue">M</i><b>Muthu · Owner</b><p>Business overview, exceptions, configuration, approvals, and refunds.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="finish"><div class="shell"><p class="kicker light">The example in one line</p><h2>A person acts. TAR checks.<br>Everything saves together.<br>The next work wakes.</h2><a href="/architecture">Explore the full technical architecture <b>→</b></a></div></section></main><footer><span>TAR v6 · Order #1042</span><a href="/architecture">Technical architecture</a></footer>
<script>import '../scripts/home.js';</script>
</Base>
